        "original_id": "3223488b-d97b-549c-8b00-375b957b946d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hal B. Wallis, Humphrey Bogart, Joel McCrea, Sylvia Sidney, Michael Curtiz, Bette Davis, Errol Flynn\n- Films: Casablanca, True Grit, The Maltese Falcon, The Big Sleep, Dead End, Trouble Along the Way\n- Companies: Warner Bros.\n- Topics: American film production, film acting, film noir\n\nFacts:\n- Hal B. Wallis, born Aaron Blum Wolowicz on October 19, 1898, was an American film producer.\n- Humphrey Bogart, born on December 25, 1899, was an American screen and stage actor.\n- Dead End is a 1937 film that stars Humphrey Bogart, Joel McCrea, and Sylvia Sidney.\n- Hal B. Wallis produced Casablanca in 1942 for Warner Bros.\n- Humphrey Bogart became a cultural icon through his performances in 1940s film noir movies including The Maltese Falcon, Casablanca, and The Big Sleep.\n- Michael Curtiz directed Casablanca.\n- Hal B. Wallis produced many major Warner Bros. films featuring stars such as Humphrey Bogart, Bette Davis, and Errol Flynn.\n- Trouble Along the Way was directed by Michael Curtiz.\n- Hal B. Wallis produced True Grit in 1969.\n- Hal B. Wallis died on October 5, 1986.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
