        "text": "Page: Hal B. Wallis. Sentence: Harold Brent Wallis (born Aaron Blum Wolowicz; October 19, 1898 – October 5, 1986) was an American film producer.\nPage: Hal B. Wallis. Sentence: He is best remembered for producing \"Casablanca\" (1942) and \"True Grit\" (1969), along with many other major films for Warner Bros. featuring such film stars as Humphrey Bogart, Bette Davis, and Errol Flynn.\nPage: Humphrey Bogart. Sentence: Humphrey DeForest Bogart ( ; December 25, 1899January 14, 1957) was an American screen and stage actor whose performances in 1940s films noir such as \"The Maltese Falcon\", \"Casablanca\", and \"The Big Sleep\" earned him status as a cultural icon.\nPage: Dead End (1937 film). Sentence: It stars Humphrey Bogart, Joel McCrea, and Sylvia Sidney.\nPage: Trouble Along the Way. Sentence: The movie was directed by Michael Curtiz, director of \"Casablanca\".",
